1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,139
Hit a cricket ball high.

2
00:00:02,139 --> 00:00:05,807
It rises, slows, and falls
back along one smooth curve.

3
00:00:06,207 --> 00:00:08,716
Now look at a dish antenna on a roof.

4
00:00:08,716 --> 00:00:13,135
Its metal bowl has the very same
curve, and it sends every signal to one

5
00:00:13,135 --> 00:00:14,656
point in front of it.

6
00:00:15,106 --> 00:00:17,575
Aarav spotted both on his ride to college.

7
00:00:17,925 --> 00:00:20,010
A flying ball and a metal dish.

8
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:21,897
Why do they share one curve?

9
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:24,183
That curve is the parabola.

10
00:00:24,183 --> 00:00:26,607
And one simple rule builds all of it.

11
00:00:27,257 --> 00:00:28,430
Here is the rule.

12
00:00:28,430 --> 00:00:33,017
Take a fixed point, called the focus,
and a fixed line, called the directrix.

13
00:00:33,417 --> 00:00:37,998
A parabola is the set of all points
that are the same distance from the

14
00:00:37,998 --> 00:00:40,034
focus and from the directrix.

15
00:00:40,434 --> 00:00:41,860
Watch the test run.

16
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:46,406
A point moves so that its distance to
the focus always equals its distance

17
00:00:46,406 --> 00:00:47,426
to the line.

18
00:00:47,826 --> 00:00:48,815
Five and five.

19
00:00:48,815 --> 00:00:49,891
Eight and eight.

20
00:00:49,891 --> 00:00:53,810
Every point that passes leaves a
dot, and the dots trace the curve.

21
00:00:54,210 --> 00:00:58,575
The line through the focus, square
to the directrix, is the axis.

22
00:00:58,575 --> 00:01:02,792
The curve meets the axis at the
vertex, halfway between the two.

23
00:01:03,442 --> 00:01:04,432
Remember this.

24
00:01:04,432 --> 00:01:08,878
Every point on a parabola is as far
from the focus as from the directrix.

25
00:01:09,578 --> 00:01:10,881
Now the equation.

26
00:01:10,881 --> 00:01:15,821
Put the vertex at the origin, the
focus at a, zero, and the directrix at

27
00:01:15,821 --> 00:01:17,186
x equals minus a.

28
00:01:17,586 --> 00:01:18,486
Step one.

29
00:01:18,387 --> 00:01:23,441
The distance from P to the focus is the
square root of, x minus a all squared,

30
00:01:23,441 --> 00:01:24,594
plus y squared.

31
00:01:25,344 --> 00:01:26,244
Step two.

32
00:01:26,152 --> 00:01:30,516
The distance from P to the directrix
is straight across: x plus a.

33
00:01:31,266 --> 00:01:32,166
Step three.

34
00:01:32,113 --> 00:01:35,667
Set them equal, and square
both sides to remove the root.

35
00:01:36,417 --> 00:01:37,317
Step four.

36
00:01:37,076 --> 00:01:38,713
Open the brackets on each side.

37
00:01:39,463 --> 00:01:40,363
Step five.

38
00:01:40,287 --> 00:01:44,186
x squared and a squared appear
on both sides, so they cancel.

39
00:01:44,186 --> 00:01:46,978
What is left is y squared equals four a x.

40
00:01:47,628 --> 00:01:48,925
Now the live part.

41
00:01:48,925 --> 00:01:51,910
a is the distance from
the vertex to the focus.

42
00:01:52,309 --> 00:01:53,921
Grow a from one to three.

43
00:01:53,921 --> 00:01:57,394
The focus moves out, and the
parabola opens wider and wider.

44
00:01:58,044 --> 00:01:59,094
One more length.

45
00:01:59,094 --> 00:02:02,959
The latus rectum is the chord through
the focus, square to the axis.

46
00:02:03,359 --> 00:02:04,563
Put x equals a.

47
00:02:04,563 --> 00:02:08,786
Then y squared is four a squared,
so y is plus or minus two a.

48
00:02:09,536 --> 00:02:13,140
From minus two a up to two
a, its length is four a.

49
00:02:13,790 --> 00:02:14,846
Side by side.

50
00:02:14,846 --> 00:02:18,786
In y squared equals four a x,
the letter x is not squared.

51
00:02:18,786 --> 00:02:22,882
So the axis is the x axis, and
the curve opens to the right.

52
00:02:23,282 --> 00:02:26,744
In x squared equals four
a y, y is not squared.

53
00:02:26,744 --> 00:02:29,783
The axis is the y axis, and it opens up.

54
00:02:29,783 --> 00:02:33,503
A minus sign flips each
one, to the left, or down.

55
00:02:34,103 --> 00:02:35,003
Your turn.

56
00:02:34,958 --> 00:02:37,083
x squared equals minus eight y.

57
00:02:37,083 --> 00:02:40,328
Which way does it open,
and where is the focus?

58
00:02:40,328 --> 00:02:41,587
Pause and decide.

59
00:02:44,787 --> 00:02:47,911
Down, with the focus at zero, minus two!

60
00:02:47,911 --> 00:02:51,334
y is not squared, so
the axis is the y axis.

61
00:02:51,334 --> 00:02:52,976
The minus means down.

62
00:02:52,976 --> 00:02:55,685
And four a is eight, so a is two.

63
00:02:56,335 --> 00:02:58,025
Now, one worked example.

64
00:02:58,375 --> 00:03:02,796
For y squared equals twelve x, find
the focus, the directrix and the latus

65
00:03:02,796 --> 00:03:03,696
rectum.

66
00:03:03,906 --> 00:03:04,806
Step one.

67
00:03:04,627 --> 00:03:07,081
Match it with y squared equals four a x.

68
00:03:07,081 --> 00:03:09,218
Four a is twelve, so a is three.

69
00:03:09,968 --> 00:03:10,868
Step two.

70
00:03:10,793 --> 00:03:12,704
The focus is three, zero.

71
00:03:12,704 --> 00:03:15,289
The directrix is x equals minus three.

72
00:03:16,039 --> 00:03:16,939
Step three.

73
00:03:16,843 --> 00:03:19,545
The latus rectum is
four a, which is twelve.

74
00:03:20,295 --> 00:03:24,498
Check: the point three, six is on the
curve, since six squared and twelve

75
00:03:24,498 --> 00:03:26,417
times three are both thirty six.

76
00:03:26,417 --> 00:03:28,527
It is one end of the latus rectum.

77
00:03:29,177 --> 00:03:30,638
Now, the exam trap.

78
00:03:30,988 --> 00:03:32,741
y squared equals eight x.

79
00:03:32,741 --> 00:03:35,849
Many students say the
focus is at eight, zero.

80
00:03:36,249 --> 00:03:38,465
But eight is four a, not a.

81
00:03:38,465 --> 00:03:41,874
So a is two, and the
focus is at two, zero.

82
00:03:42,524 --> 00:03:43,893
Where is this asked?

83
00:03:43,893 --> 00:03:44,840
In JEE Main.

84
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:49,059
In August twenty twenty one, a question
gave the vertex and the focus of

85
00:03:49,059 --> 00:03:51,798
a parabola, and asked
for its latus rectum.

86
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:53,584
Exam level now.

87
00:03:53,584 --> 00:03:58,787
On y squared equals four a x, a point
P has x equal to four, and its distance

88
00:03:58,787 --> 00:04:00,445
from the focus is six.

89
00:04:00,445 --> 00:04:02,042
Find the latus rectum.

90
00:04:02,042 --> 00:04:03,278
Pause and solve.

91
00:04:08,678 --> 00:04:10,088
The answer is C.

92
00:04:10,088 --> 00:04:10,988
Eight.

93
00:04:11,255 --> 00:04:15,100
By the rule, P is as far from
the focus as from the directrix.

94
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:20,196
The directrix is x equals minus a,
so that distance is four plus a.

95
00:04:20,696 --> 00:04:23,472
Four plus a equals six, so a is two.

96
00:04:23,472 --> 00:04:26,608
The latus rectum is
four a, which is eight.

97
00:04:27,208 --> 00:04:28,748
Here is your recap.

98
00:04:28,748 --> 00:04:30,331
Screenshot this card.

99
00:04:33,531 --> 00:04:35,717
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

100
00:04:36,117 --> 00:04:37,017
One.

101
00:04:36,615 --> 00:04:40,636
Every point on a parabola is
equally far from which two things?

102
00:04:41,536 --> 00:04:42,436
Two.

103
00:04:41,992 --> 00:04:44,897
Where is the focus of x
squared equals twenty y?

104
00:04:45,797 --> 00:04:46,697
Three.

105
00:04:46,366 --> 00:04:49,446
Which way does y squared
equals minus six x open?

106
00:04:50,546 --> 00:04:55,331
Next time: a loop of string, two pins
and a pencil draw a perfect oval.

107
00:04:55,331 --> 00:04:56,231
How?

108
00:04:55,829 --> 00:04:56,776
The ellipse.
